WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
<v Priya Raman>Weekly status. Wave 1 is stable, no incidents this week.</v>

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Good. On wave 2, two more regions asked to join, so it may be 52 stores instead of 48.</v>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.000
<v Priya Raman>That would need a change to CR-02, since it was priced for 48. When will you know?</v>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>I should hear by October 16.</v>

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Lena Ortiz>Also, the store managers want the cutover on a Thursday night, not a Wednesday. Weekends are too busy and Wednesdays have deliveries.</v>

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Let's look at moving it. November 12 is a Thursday, right?</v>

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Priya Raman>Yes, November 12 is a Thursday. We'd need a week to re-plan, but it's possible.</v>

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.000
<v Jordan Alvarez>Then let's tentatively move to November 12. I'll confirm next week.</v>

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
<v Tom Becker>Security update: we'll send the card reader list by October 10 as promised.</v>

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Priya Raman>Thanks Tom. And Lena, the runbook version 0.3 with the store checklist went out on October 3.</v>

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Lena Ortiz>Got it, the managers liked the checklist.</v>
